      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=3{x}^{4}+12{x}^{2}+2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(1,17)?$",
      "worked_solution": "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+12{x}^{2}+2{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3{x}^{3}+2\\cdot 12x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}+24x+{x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & =12(1)^{3}+24(1)+(1)^{-1/2} \\\\  & =12+24+1 \\\\  & =37.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $37.$",
