      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the exact value of the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+12x$ whose tangent has a slope of $0.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+12x.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+12x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-12x+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-12x+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $0$ at the point where $x=2.$",
